          <p class="kicker">{{ focus.eyebrow }}</p>
          <h2>{{ focus.label }}</h2>
          {% if focus.key == 'integration' %}
            <p class="focus-pillar-thesis">A self is proposed not as a finished object but as a repeatedly renewed act of integration. Differentiation supplies what the next integration must gather.</p>
            <p>The expression \(I_{n+1}=\mathcal{R}(I_n,D_n)\) names that conjecture. It is a schematic research commitment, not yet a physical law. Part I tests its mathematical vocabulary, its account of the self, its thermodynamic debt and its cosmological consequences.</p>
          {% elif focus.key == 'splice' %}
            <p class="focus-pillar-thesis">At a density threshold, the Rankin Skeletal Splice proposes a fork: one branch continues while one returns, framed by the fixed skeleton \(-1,0,1\).</p>
            <p>Given the idealised rule, \(P_n=F_{n+2}-1\) is mathematically checkable. Its promotion into gravity, matter, scale or cosmology remains conjectural. Part II therefore moves from gravity and accumulation through the exact recurrence to toroidal return structures.</p>
          {% else %}
            <p class="focus-pillar-thesis">Return requires geometry. Seams, inversions and temporal antipodes are examined as possible models of re-entry without treating infinity as a distant wall.</p>
            <p>The Möbius identification \((x,0)\sim(1-x,1)\) is established topology. A cosmic seam, inherited residue or temporal return is not. Part III keeps those proposals beside entropy, conservation, causality and observational constraints.</p>
          {% endif %}
