<section class="wrap reveal" aria-labelledby="testable-joins-title">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Four Joins, Revisited · Four New Joins</p>
    <h2 id="testable-joins-title">Where the Framework Touches Something Testable</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">r3.5 named four places where geometry reached toward a measured thing. They are restored first, with the qualifications subsequent work required, followed by four later joins. None is counted as established physics.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid two">
    <article class="frame card card--linked">
      <h3><a class="card-link" href="/moebius/#t-colour">The seam and the colour charge</a></h3>
      <p>Colour confinement invited comparison between a charge never exhibited alone and one-sided identification. The Z₂ twist and Z₃ colour structure are a resemblance to be derived or rejected, not a definition of the strong force.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card card--linked">
      <h3><a class="card-link" href="/moebius/#t-handedness">Whether galaxies carry a rotation bias</a></h3>
      <p>The historical 158-to-105 count and a reported dipole motivated an odd great-circle prediction. Classification, selection and coordinate-system effects must be controlled before any cosmic twist is inferred.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card card--linked">
      <h3><a class="card-link" href="/cosmic-ledger/#t-dark-matter">Dark matter as the ledger&rsquo;s middle entry</a></h3>
      <p>The 26.95 percent value was placed at the π/2 pole and read as integration sufficient to curve without shining. That is a fitted interpretation until it outperforms particle, modified-gravity and structure-formation accounts.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card card--linked">
      <h3><a class="card-link" href="/spiral/#t-quarks">The thirty-six, the quarks and the pace</a></h3>
      <p>\(666=T_{36}\), while six flavours, three colours and two signs give thirty-six labels. The arithmetic is exact; its physical salience, and the move from triangular increments to a harmonic pace, remain conjectural.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card card--linked">
      <h3><a class="card-link" href="/little-red-dots/research-proposal/">The Zero-Seam Test</a></h3>
      <p>A staged protocol compares conventional compact-source models, a local propagation front and inherited boundary residue. Every model is given a route to lose.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card card--linked">
      <h3><a class="card-link" href="/cosmic-ratio-in-time/">Sector exchange through cosmic time</a></h3>
      <p>Changing density fractions do not by themselves prove conversion. Physical exchange requires source terms that conserve the total ledger and improve on ordinary expansion.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card card--linked">
      <h3><a class="card-link" href="/accumulated-differentials/">Accumulation, mass and gravity</a></h3>
      <p>Exact finite sums are not yet a gravitational theory. A viable bridge must specify dimensions, a covariant source, field equations and independent predictions for motion and lensing.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card card--linked">
      <h3><a class="card-link" href="/riemann-splice-questions/">The splice after the Riemann audit</a></h3>
      <p>The RH archive supplies diagnostics and correction discipline; it does not derive the splice coefficient, an action, a gravitational scale or electromagnetic normalisation.</p>
    </article>
