<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="kicker">The standing rule of this site</p>
    <h2 id="t-earned-chosen-refused">Earned, Chosen, Refused</h2>
    <p>Every chapter of the restored Unified Edition closed with <em>What Is Earned and What Is Chosen</em>, and every page keeps that habit. <strong>Earned</strong> means an identity, deduction or observation can be checked under stated assumptions. <strong>Chosen</strong> means an interpretation is coherent but not forced. <strong>Refused</strong> means a dramatic claim was available and was withheld or downgraded because its proof, mechanism or evidence is not yet present.</p>
    <p>The integrated edition adds a fourth discipline: <strong>corrected</strong>. Later audits govern earlier confidence. Exact mathematics does not become empirical proof merely because it fits the framework&rsquo;s preferred picture.</p>
    <p class="muted">A reader who cannot tell the theorem from the vision has not been given the research; they have been given a mood.</p>
  </div>
</section>

